  '[{"id": "a", "text": "rare diseases"}, {"id": "b", "text": "very common diseases only"}, {"id": "c", "text": "the long-term effects of a treatment given by random allocation"}, {"id": "d", "text": "the prevalence of a disease in a community"}]'::jsonb, 'a', 'It starts with the cases, so a large cohort is not needed to find enough cases. It measures an odds ratio.', 3,
